"'''Stone Soup'''" is a European [[Folklore|folk story]] in which hungry strangers convince the people of a town to each share a small amount of their food in order to make a meal. In varying traditions, the stone has been replaced with other common inedible objects, and therefore the parable is also known as '''axe soup''', '''button soup''', '''nail soup''', '''bolt soup''', and '''wood soup'''.
